  "releaseNotes": "# AID v2.2.0\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n- 新增默认关闭的错误诊断与日志报告发送。服务端、后台和 Web 可关联同一请求及异步任务，保留脱敏后的供应商错误与浏览器证据；管理员在服务器出口 IP 获授权后，可将报告加密送达官方，查看异步发送结果并人工重试未确认报告。不会自动上传全部服务器日志，也不会重试原业务生成请求。\n- 修复并发请求和定时任务可能引起的注解缓存死锁；改进供应商欠费与鉴权错误的区分。\n- 扩充图片编辑模型能力与业务配置，支持蒙版选区、扩图、打光、输出尺寸和多结果幂等保存；能力模板只补齐缺项，新增能力默认停用，不更改既有报价。\n- 模型可选配图片输入 URL 代理模板；未启用时保持原有资源签名方式。视频参考模式支持参考音色 ID，模型接口向 Web 返回当前业务的提示词字符上限。\n- 后台优化模型池候选与参数提示、视频能力设置和长列表横向浏览；Web 编辑弹窗按模型能力校验提示词长度，项目详情及诊断状态请求避免重复提交。\n- 修正仍使用旧版错误默认值的交流二维码资源路径；管理员自定义地址保持不变。\n- 数据库升级执行 `sql/v2.2.0.sql`。已在隔离 MySQL 5.7 库验证从最早公开的 `v1.0.0-beta.1` 按顺序升级，以及本版 SQL 重复执行；升级前仍需备份数据库、配置与用户媒体，并在维护窗口暂停媒体任务写入。\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n- Added opt-in error diagnostics and encrypted report delivery. Server, admin, and Web evidence is correlated by request and task. After the server's outbound IP is authorized, administrators can send a sanitized report, inspect asynchronous delivery, and manually retry an unconfirmed report. This does not upload all server logs or retry the original generation request.\n- Fixed a possible annotation-cache deadlock under concurrent requests and scheduled tasks, and distinguished provider credit exhaustion from authentication failures.\n- Expanded image-edit model capabilities and business configuration for masks, expansion, relighting, output dimensions, and idempotent multi-result storage. New capabilities remain disabled by default; existing pricing is preserved.\n- Added optional image-input URL proxy templates, reference voice IDs for video scenes, and model-specific prompt limits exposed to Web editors.\n- Improved model-pool validation, video capability settings, and horizontal navigation in long admin tables. Web editors enforce the selected model's prompt limit and coalesce duplicate project-detail and diagnostic requests.\n- Corrected only the legacy default community QR-code path; administrator-defined URLs remain unchanged.\n- Apply `sql/v2.2.0.sql` when upgrading. An isolated MySQL 5.7 test covered the ordered chain from `v1.0.0-beta.1` and repeat execution. Back up data, configuration, and user media first, and pause media writes during migration.",
